{
  "manufacturer": "Swegon",
  "manufacturer_slug": "swegon",
  "model": "TAC6 controller (Global units)",
  "model_slug": "tac6-modbus",
  "short_model": "TAC6",
  "aliases": [
    "Global TAC6",
    "SAT WIFI-ETHERNET (TAC6)"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Air handler (heat recovery unit controller)",
  "applies_to": "Swegon (Global) units with the TAC6 regulation board and a Modbus satellite; TAC6 + MODBUS TABLE Cid 050360 (2021-05-20).",
  "summary": "TAC6 is the newer controller of Swegon/Global heat recovery units. All data is in signed 16-bit holding registers: identification, working mode and speed, fan flows, pressures and RPM, temperatures T1-T8, input/output states, run and maintenance hours, alarm bitmaps and the Modbus control block for speed, airflows, bypass, boost and fire alarm. This map lists the registers an integrator needs, not every setup parameter.",
  "transport": [
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The table prints 4xxxx registers. Swegon's TAC6 + Modbus TCP/IP manual (French) says the leading 4 is only a type prefix and that document numbering is one-based while the address sent is zero-based (register 41001 is sent as 1000). So 40201 is holding register 200 on the wire."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "TAC6 + MODBUS TABLE - Installation and user's manual",
    "doc_number": "Cid 050360",
    "revision_date": "2021-05-20",
    "url": "https://pre.swegon.com/globalassets/digizuite/11951-en-global_tac6_modbustable_regulation_installation_en.pdf",
    "pages": "register tables in section 4 (general info, visualization, control, alarms, setup). Offset, signedness and 32-bit word order: TAC6 + MODBUS TCP/IP manual (French, https://pre.swegon.com/globalassets/digizuite/11940-en-global_tac6_sat_modbustcpip_installation_fr.pdf)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Addressing and word order come from Swegon's French manual 'TAC6 + MODBUS TCP/IP' (050325, 2023-07-14), which is written for TAC6 boards in GLOBAL/ESENSA units; the register table itself does not repeat them.",
    "The TAC6 TCP/IP manual states that all values are signed and that 32-bit values are sent low word first, then high word (Val32 = HIGH x 65536 + LOW), so 32-bit registers here are INT32 CDAB. When writing a 32-bit value, write the low word first; the value updates when the high word arrives.",
    "Only a selection is listed: the general info, visualization, control and alarm blocks plus the working mode, flow ratio and Modbus address setup registers. Setup, advanced setup and time-table registers (40400-41xxx) are left out; see the source table.",
    "The TAC6 TCP/IP manual says setup parameters are stored in EEPROM rated for about 1,000,000 write cycles; the TAC6 table does not mark which registers these are, so do not write setup values cyclically.",
    "Flow values are m³/h or % of maximum torque depending on the working mode (CA vs TQ); 40055 gives the unit of 40054.",
    "The TAC6 table does not give where each probe T1-T8 sits in the unit. The digital input/output bitmaps differ from TAC5."
  ],
